    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `salutation` feature to the PetClinic REST app, following the existing derived-field conventions (like `displayName`/`initials`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema (documented values MR/MRS/MS/DR) and a read-only `salutation` field to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs are regenerated from this at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `title` column (getter/setter) and a `@Transient getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/blank.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", expression = \"java(owner.getSalutation())\")` so the response carries it. The inbound `title` is auto-mapped by name into the entity.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added a `title` column to the `owners` table so the value persists across the create \u2192 GET round-trip (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (POST with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 `GET` expecting `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
