    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's established patterns cleanly:\n\n- **`getSalutation()` on the `Owner` entity** matches the existing, well-populated pattern of `@Transient` derived read-only getters on this entity (`getAgeBand()`, `getMembershipPoints()`, `getMembershipLevel()`, `getCheckDigit()`, `getIdentityKey()`). Deriving `salutation` from the entity's own persisted fields (`title` + inherited `lastName`) belongs right here, and a maintainer would expect to find it alongside its siblings.\n- **The persisted `title` field** is added with its `@Column` getter/setter in the natural place, and is wired consistently across all four schema dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n- **The mapper mapping** `expression = \"java(owner.getSalutation())\"` mirrors how the mapper already consumes entity-owned derivations (e.g. `ageBand` delegates to `owner.getAgeBand()`; it only routes through a helper because it needs a String\u2192enum conversion, which `salutation` as a plain String does not). No new mapper helper is warranted, so nothing is duplicated and the mapper doesn't accrete needless methods.\n- **OpenAPI** documents both the inbound `title` (on the fields schema) and the read-only `salutation` (on the DTO, `readOnly: true`), consistent with how the other derived fields are described.\n\nNothing is in the wrong unit, duplicated, or turning a class into a catch-all. The structure is additive and idiomatic.",
